  "parApproaches": {
    "_comment": "PAR approaches per runway end (docs/adr/0112), read once at start-up, never written by code (P5). EVERY VALUE IS [SOURCE-DEFINED] and only a DEFAULT: the PAR controller sets TDZE, TCH, decision height and glidepath angle at run time per runway end (docs/adr/0130, decisions H153; no LTAG plate is owed). thresholdLat/Lon: the landing threshold as DCS places it: the squadron mission's RW05 and RW23 nav points (STT v21, DCS x/z 220339.7/-36479.7 and 222075.4/-34001.1) through the Syria Transverse Mercator projection; they agree to about 35 m with the real thresholds (36.9937 N 35.4122 E, 37.0103 N 35.4395 E). courseTrueDeg: the final approach course, degrees TRUE, the geodesic bearing threshold to threshold (52.7, reciprocal 232.7; the real runway is 52.9 true), equal to the runway's endHeadingsTrue and shown magnetic through the theater's variation (U-LTAG-COURSE: the earlier 56 was the runway number read as magnetic, 3.3 degrees off the pavement). tdzeFt: touchdown zone elevation, feet MSL; null takes the DCS airfield's elevation, which is what the aircraft fly over in DCS (the real LTAG is 238 ft). tchFt: threshold crossing height (50 ft, the usual figure). decisionHeightFt: decision height above TDZE (200 ft, HAT; DA = TDZE + this). glideslopeDeg: the published glidepath angle, or null for none, in which case par.json's defaultGlideslopeDeg applies (H116: 3.06).",
